    "chunk_text": "shall be prima facie evidence of the facts statedtherein and the pure quantity of such dangerousdrug shall be deemed to be not exceeding twogrammes.\n\nShort title\n\nAmendment ofsection 54A ofChapter 218\n\n[Certified on 23rd of November, 2022]\n\n2Poisons, Opium and Dangerous Drugs(Amendment) Act, No. 41 of 2022\n\n(3) In this section -\n\n\u201cmanufacture\u201d in relation to a dangerousdrug includes any process ofproducing such drug and therefining or transformation of onedrug into another;\n\n\u201ctraffick\u201d means-\n\n(a)to sell, give, procure, store,administer, transport, send,deliver or distribute; or\n\n(b)to offer to do anythingspecified in paragraph (a).\u201d.\n\n3. Section 77A of the principal enactment is herebyamended as follows: -\n\n(1) by the repeal of subsections (2), (3) and (4) of thatsection and the substitution therefor of thefollowing: -\n\n\u201c(2) Where the Government Analyst hasmade an examination of any drug, substance,article or preparation submitted to him under\n\nAmendment ofsection 77A ofthe principalenactment\n\n3Poisons, Opium and Dangerous Drugs(Amendment) Act, No. 41 of 2022\n\nsubsection (1), he shall, within a period not exceeding twelve months from the date of such submission, send a report setting out the result of his examination to the Magistrate or any other competent court which has the jurisdiction to try an offence committed under Chapter III or Chapter V of this Ordinance, with copies to the police officer who submitted such drug, substance, article and preparation or any portion or sample for examination and to the Police Narcotics Bureau.\n\n(3) A report submitted to the Magistrate or any other competent court under subsection (2) shall be prima facie evidence in any inquiry, trial or other proceeding conducted under this Ordinance."
