    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 8.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka of January 22, 2021\n\nThis Act can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\n[Certified on 18th of January, 2021]\n\nINTELLECTUAL PROPERTY (AMENDMENT)ACT, No. 8 OF 2021\n\nIntellectual Property (Amendment)Act, No. 8 of 20211\n\n[Certified on 18th of January, 2021]\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 11/2016\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE INTELLECTUAL PROPERTYACT, NO.36 OF 2003\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Intellectual Property(Amendment) Act, No. 8 of 2021.\n\n2.Section 5 of the Intellectual Property Act, No. 36 of2003 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) ishereby amended as follows:\u2014\n\n(1)by the insertion immediately before the definitionof the expression \u201caudiovisual work\u201d, of thefollowing definition:\u2013\n\n\u2018\u201caccessible format\u201d means a copy of a work in analternative form or manner which gives abeneficiary person access to such work,including to permit such person to have accessas feasibly and comfortably as a personwithout any disability which a beneficiaryperson has. The accessible format copy shallbe used exclusively by beneficiary personsand shall respect the intergrity of the originalwork, taking into consideration of the changesneeded to make the work accessible in thealternative format and of the accessibilityneeds of the beneficiary person;\u201d.\n\nShort title\n\nAmendment ofsection 5 of Act,No. 36 of 2003\n\n2Intellectual Property (Amendment)Act, No. 8 of 2021\n\n(2)by the insertion immediately after the definition ofthe expression \u201cauthor\u201d of the followingdefinition:\u2013\n\n\u201c \u201cbeneficiary person\u201d means any person who\u2013\n\n(a) is blind;"
