    "chunk_text": "PRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 6.00 Postage : Rs. 10.00\n\nPARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\nPublished as a Supplement to Part II of the Gazette of the DemocraticSocialist Republic of Sri Lanka of February 23, 2017\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Certified on 22nd February, 2017]\n\nPrinted on the Order of Government\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nLAND (RESTRICTIONS ON ALIENATION)(AMENDMENT) ACT, No. 3 OF 2017\n\nLand (Restrictions on Alienation) (Amendment)Act, No. 3 of 20171\n\n2\u2014PL 010272\u20142,961 (01/2016)\n\n[Certified on 22nd February, 2017]\n\nL.D.\u2014O. 14/2016\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE LAND (RESTRICTIONS ON ALIENATION)ACT, NO. 38 OF 2014\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Land (Restrictions onAlienation) (Amendment) Act, No. 3 of 2017 and shall bedeemed to have come into operation with effect fromJanuary 8, 2017.\n\n2.The following new section is hereby insertedimmediately after section 5 of the Land (Restrictions onAlienation) Act, No. 38 of 2014 and shall have effect assection 5A of that Act:\u2014\n\n5A. Notwithstanding anything to the contraryin any of the provisions of this Act, theprovisions relating to the Land Lease Tax shallnot apply to a lease of any land\u2014\n\n(a)to a foreigner; or\n\n(b)to a company incorporated in Sri Lankaunder the Companies Act, where anyforeign shareholding in such company,either direct or indirect, is fifty per centor above; or\n\n(c)to a foreign company,\n\nunder and indenture of lease executed on orafter January 8, 2017, and accordingly the LandLease Tax shall not be charged, levied orcollected from any such person or company onor after such date.\u201d.\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nShort title anddate ofoperation.\n\nInsertion of newsection 5A in Act,No. 38 of 2014."
